N eclplot.pkg
D 20 Mar 2025
U 115
d 'ECLPLOT': module to generate estimates and confidence limits plots
d 
d    eclplot creates a plot of estimates with lower and upper
d confidence limits  on one axis against another numeric
d variable on the other axis. The estimates  and lower and
d upper confidence limits are stored in three variables, in a
d data set with one observation per confidence interval to be
d plotted. Data      sets with such variables may be created
d manually (using a  spreadsheet), or using the parmest
d package, or using statsby or postfile in official Stata.
d  The user has a choice of plotting the confidence intervals
d horizontally or      vertically, a choice of plot styles for the
d estimates, and a choice of range plot styles for the
d confidence intervals. It is also possible to overlay     the
d confidence interval plot with other plots using the plot()
d option,      and to overlay multiple superimposed confidence
d interval plots using the supby() option. eclplot may be used
d either as a command or through a dialog.
d 
d KW: estimation results
d KW: confidence intervals
d KW: graphics
d 
d Requires: Stata version 13
d 
