N xtdpdgmm.pkg
D  4 Oct 2026
U 172
d 'XTDPDGMM': module to perform generalized method of moments estimation of linear dynamic panel data models
d 
d  xtdpdgmm implements generalized method of moments estimators for
d linear dynamic panel models. Linear moment conditions in the
d spirit of Arellano and Bond (1991), Arellano and Bover (1995),
d Blundell and Bond (1998), and Hayakawa, Qi, and Breitung (2019)
d can be combined with the nonlinear moment conditions suggested by
d Ahn and Schmidt (1995) or Chudik and Pesaran (2022). One-step,
d two-step, iterated, and continuously-updating GMM estimators can
d be used. The Windmeijer (2005) finite-sample standard error
d correction and the doubly-corrected misspecification-robust
d standard errors of Hwang, Kang, and Lee (2022) are available.
d Possible model transformations include first differences,
d deviations from within-group means, and forward-orthogonal
d deviations. Available postestimation statistics include the
d Arellano and Bond (1991) and Jochmans (2020) tests for
d autocorrelation of the residuals, the Sargan-Hansen test for the
d validity of the overidentifying restrictions, a generalized
d Hausman test, and the Andrews and Lu (2001) model and moment
d selection criteria.
d 
d KW: dynamic panel data
d KW: generalized method of moments
d 
d Requires: Stata version 13
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20220805
d 
d Author: Sebastian Kripfganz, University of Exeter
d Support: email S.Kripfganz@@exeter.ac.uk
d 
f x/xtdpdgmm.ado
f x/xtdpdgmm.sthlp
f x/xtdpdgmmfe.ado
f x/xtdpdgmmfe.sthlp
f x/xtdpdgmm_p.ado
f x/xtdpdgmm_estat.ado
f x/xtdpdgmm_postestimation.sthlp
f l/lxtdpdgmm.mlib
e
